    add();add('The 2% first-lex target was explicitly informed by the earlier H3bp 2.825688% archived-bank reduction and fixed before these fresh banks. It is a new target, not a revision of H3bp. H3bn and H3bp remain falsifications of their 5% target against first-lex. This fresh 3.984064% saving also falls below 5%; no such claim is made. The posterior comparison is a separate hypothesis with a different comparator. There is no omnibus test or claim of population significance. A zero-cost comparator was predefined as inconclusive for that endpoint.');add()
    add('All 22 selected truths receive 64 new banks. Each bank is eight distinct N12 positives sampled directly by `default_rng(2026600000 + 64*candidateID + bank).choice(M,8,replace=False)`. Direct uniform eight-sampling has the same sampling law as H3bm’s uniform sixteen-then-eight subset, using a new RNG namespace. All 1,408 sources are durably logged before any new target MAP label. There is no redrawing, filtering, deletion, seed tuning or suppression of ties, failures or duplicates. The seed audit found no collision with 7,456 explicitly recorded historical seed values; undocumented RNG streams are outside that audit.');add()
    add(f"All policies preserve the same {s['exact_cases']:,} exact cases. The {s['feasible_checkpoint_cases']:,} feasible checkpoints map to {s['distinct_feasible_sets']:,} candidate sets. The {s['infeasible_checkpoint_cases']} infeasible checkpoints and {s['prior_success_cases']} prior successes remain explicit and acquire no continuation labels. There are {s['distinct_compiled_sets']} distinct unresolved candidate sets in total. Per-case equality is required by the common feasible depth-four tree class; it is a correctness invariant, not another scientific success or a reliability guarantee.");add()
    add('| Truth | Exact cases /64 | Infeasible cases | Prior successes | Shared MAP | First-lex continuation | Posterior continuation | Uniform continuation |');add('|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
    for r in s['truth_results']:
        c=r['continuation_calls'];add(f"| {r['candidate']} | {r['exact_cases']} | {r['infeasible_cases']} | {r['prior_success_cases']} | {r['shared_MAP_calls']} | {c['firstlex']} | {c['posterior']} | {c['uniform']} |")
    add();add('Each source bank is filtered against all 1,541 supplied candidates, including compatible models with source cardinality between eight and fifteen. The correct eight-positive score is C(55,k) C(M,8). The byte-identical MAP selector uses the lowest score, then smallest candidate ID, and the lexicographically first maximum-disagreement query. Up to four MAP queries are shared once. All shared checkpoints are completed before compiling any continuation trees.');add()
    add('The first-lex arm uses the unchanged first-feasible depth-four compiler. Both optimized arms use the byte-identical exact weighted compiler. Posterior weights are positive integers proportional to reciprocal eight-positive scores; uniform weights are exactly one for every remaining candidate. Complete N13 signature catalogs cover all 73,712 ordinary boards. Optimal cost ties use the first lexicographic board. All policy inputs bind the candidate set, weights, depth, catalog hash, predictions hash and compiler hash; grouping identical candidate sets occurs only within these fixed inputs. Compilers receive no case or true identity.');add()
